      en: ["Part of the Bas-Ogooué Ramsar site, designated in 2009.", "The lake is located in the Moyen-Ogooué Province of western Gabon.", "It serves as a critical water reservoir during the dry season.", "The ecosystem hosts the rare African manatee in its waters.", "Traditional fishing provides the main livelihood for local people.", "The lake is connected directly to the Ogooué River via channels."],
